From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:45:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 104/159] [ae-patch] Size shortcut key chips to their label and
 hide the New session chip when the row is too narrow

CompactKbd was a fixed 16 px square, which fits a single glyph on macOS
but not Ctrl or Alt on Windows and Linux, so the labels spilled into each
other ("CtrlAlt N"). The chip now keeps a 16 px minimum and grows with
its label. At its real width the New session chip would cover the row's
label in a narrow sidebar, so the row is a container and the chip only
shows when the row is at least 13rem wide.
